# minimum qore version
%requires qore >= 2.0

# require type definitions everywhere

# enable all warnings

# don't use "$" for vars, members, and methods, assume local variable scope
%modern

# the heartbeat thread refers to its client by a weak reference
%allow-weak-references

# do not ignore argument errors

%requires(reexport) Mime >= 1.3
%requires(reexport) WebSocketClient >= 1.3.1
%requires(reexport) ConnectionProvider >= 1.4
%requires AsyncSocketIo
%requires HttpClientIo
%requires Util

%requires json

module DiscordWebSocketClient {
    version = "1.2";
    desc = "User module for communicating with the Discord WebSocket API gateway";
    author = "David Nichols <david@qore.org>";
    url = "https://qore.org";
    license = "MIT";
    init = sub () {
        ConnectionSchemeCache::registerScheme("discordwss", DiscordWebSocketConnection::ConnectionScheme);
    };
    # the module registers process-wide functionality in its initialization (connection schemes, LLM provider factories)
    domains = "PROCESS_CONTROL";
}

/** @mainpage DiscordWebSocketClient Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section discordwebsocketclientintro DiscordWebSocketClient Introduction

    The %DiscordWebSocketClient module provides an API for communicating with the Discord WebSocket API gateway.

    To use this module, use \c "%requires DiscordWebSocketClient" in your code.

    All the public symbols in the module are defined in the DiscordWebSocketClient namespace.

    The main classes are:
    - @ref DiscordWebSocketClient::DiscordWebSocketClient "DiscordWebSocketClient":
      this class provides the WEBSOCKET client API for communuication with the Discord WEBSOCKET
      API; it also automates authentication and authorization to the target
    - @ref DiscordWebSocketClient::DiscordWebSocketConnection "DiscordWebSocketConnection":
      provides a WEBSOCKET connection object to Discord cloud services (based on the
      @ref connectionproviderintro "ConnectionProvider" module)

    @section discordwebsocketclientrelnotes Release Notes

    @subsection discordwebsocketclientv1_2 DiscordWebSocketClient v1.2
    - fixed a heartbeat that could stall when its next beat was due in less than a millisecond; a cancelled heartbeat
      thread reports its end, so a disconnect or the destructor does not wait for it forever
    - an automatic reconnect stops the heartbeat and switches to the resume gateway URL only if no connection was
      opened after the connection it was started for ended; before, it could stop the heartbeat of the new
      connection and change the URL while it was being connected
    - an explicit @ref DiscordWebSocketClient::DiscordWebSocketClient::disconnect() "disconnect()" stops the
      heartbeat and the watchdogs once it is its turn; one that times out waiting for another connect, disconnect or
      reconnect leaves them running with the connection
    - @ref WebSocketClient::EVENT_WS_CONNECTED is raised for each connection; its report is started before the
      connection's data and close events are reported
    - the heartbeat, the HELLO watchdog and the RESUME watchdog belong to one connection: the close of a connection,
      also one reported after a newer connection was opened, stops only its own; a HELLO of a newer connection
      restarts the heartbeat with a fresh acknowledgement state; a HELLO of a connection that is no longer the
      client's is ignored
    - the HELLO watchdog is armed when a connection becomes the client's, so its timeout no longer includes the wait
      for another connect or the close of the replaced connection, and a connect that waits for another one or fails
      no longer cancels the watchdog of the connection the client has; it is also armed for connections made with
      @ref WebSocketClient::WebSocketClient::startPollConnect() "startPollConnect()"
    - a reconnect forced by the heartbeat or a watchdog is made only if the connection it was forced for is still the
      client's, so it no longer closes a newer connection or reopens a connection closed by an explicit
      @ref DiscordWebSocketClient::DiscordWebSocketClient::disconnect() "disconnect()"; a watchdog timer that fired
      before the watchdog was re-armed does nothing
    - @ref WebSocketClient::EVENT_WS_CLOSED is raised again when a connection is closed (also the data provider's
      disconnection event)
    - a HELLO watchdog that cannot be armed no longer fails the connect
    - the heartbeat thread no longer keeps the client alive: dropping the last reference to a connected client
      destroys and disconnects it; the destructor waits for the threads the client started for itself (a forced
      reconnect, automatic reconnects, \c connectAsync() workers), and works when the last reference is released on
      the heartbeat thread
    - changed protected API for subclasses: \c heartbeatThread() was replaced by the static \c heartbeatMain() and
      \c heartbeatBeat(); \c stopHeartbeatThread() called on the heartbeat thread tells it to stop instead of raising
      \c DISCORD-ERROR; the members \c hb_tid, \c hb_stop and \c heartbeat_cnt were replaced by
      the heartbeat record \c hb (see @ref DiscordWebSocketClient::DiscordHeartbeat "DiscordHeartbeat", internal);
      \c stopHeartbeatThread() takes an optional connection ID and returns a bool; \c armHelloWatchdog(),
      \c cancelHelloWatchdog(), \c armResumeWatchdog(), \c cancelResumeWatchdog(), \c helloWatchdogFired(),
      \c resumeWatchdogFired() and \c triggerZombieReconnect() take optional connection or generation arguments: an
      override must use the new signature to be called
    - the gateway URL is discovered with @ref httpclientiointro "HttpClientIo";
      @ref DiscordWebSocketClient::DiscordWebSocketConnection::discoverUrl() "DiscordWebSocketConnection::discoverUrl()"
      accepts an optional discovery URL and raises \c DISCORD-ERROR if the response gives no gateway URL
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/5469">issue 5469</a>)
    - fixed platform-generated connection URLs by declaring
      @ref DiscordWebSocketClient::DiscordWebSocketConnection::DefaultConnectionUrl "DiscordWebSocketConnection::DefaultConnectionUrl"
    - fixed a bug where a @ref DiscordWebSocketClient::DiscordWebSocketConnection "DiscordWebSocketConnection" created
      without a URL did not use the discovered gateway URL
    - fixed a bug where a server-initiated \c Heartbeat request (gateway opcode 1) caused an unhandled
      \c DISCORD-ERROR exception, killing the gateway connection and silently stopping event delivery;
      the client now responds immediately with a heartbeat as required by the Discord gateway protocol
    - fixed a bug where a zombied gateway connection (the gateway silently stops responding and
      acknowledging heartbeats, with no close frame) went undetected forever, silently stopping
      all event delivery with no error and no reconnect; heartbeat ACKs are now tracked and a
      missing ACK forces a reconnect (with session resume), as required by the gateway protocol
    - added a RESUME watchdog: when \c sendResume() is sent but the gateway answers with neither a
      \c RESUMED dispatch nor \c DOP_INVALID_SESSION within \c ResumeWatchdogTimeoutMs, the resume
      has silently failed; the watchdog clears the resumable session state and triggers a reconnect
      that falls back to a fresh \c IDENTIFY, recovering event delivery
    - fixed a bug where receiving \c DOP_INVALID_SESSION did not clear the session state, so the
      next reconnect tried \c sendResume() with the already-invalidated session in a permanent loop;
      session state is now cleared so the next reconnect uses \c sendIdentify()
    - fixed a Discord gateway protocol violation on every session-resume reconnect: the previous code
      sent \c RESUME pre-emptively from \c doReconnect() and then \c IDENTIFY from \c handleHello()
      unconditionally, so both messages went out per reconnect, which the gateway treats as
      ambiguous and can silently drop the session; the IDENTIFY/RESUME decision now happens only
      after \c HELLO arrives, so exactly one of them is sent per connection
    - added \c disconnect() override to stop the heartbeat thread before disconnecting, preventing
      service shutdown hangs when the heartbeat thread is started via \c start_thread

    @subsection discordwebsocketclientv1_0_1 DiscordWebSocketClient v1.0.1
    - fixed a bug handling \c HELLO messages
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4986">issue 4986</a>)

    @subsection discordwebsocketclientv1_0 DiscordWebSocketClient v1.0
    - initial release
*/

